            <ArticleTitle>Prevalence of obesity in the equine population of Saskatoon and surrounding area.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>967-970</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A retrospective study determined the prevalence of obesity and over-conditioning in horses in Saskatoon, Saskatchewan. Body condition score (BSC) was assessed for 290 horses from the Field Service practice at the Western College of Veterinary Medicine. The median BSC of horses was 6; however, 59 (20.3%) horses were classified as over-conditioned, and 24 (8.3%) as obese.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
